# A measured route stays with the node it was measured to.
#
# The client used to hold one traceroute: the path on this screen was whatever the last trace
# said, whoever was being looked at, so tracing a second node took the first one's route off the
# screen - and a restart took both. It now keeps the last route to each node and writes them to
# the card, which is what a measurement somebody waited a minute for is worth.
#
# The demo traced Echo Repeater and then Golf Cabin, in that order, so Golf is the trace the one
# slot is still holding and Echo's route comes back out of the log. The two screens here are the
# two halves of that: under the old single slot the first of them was blank.
#
# The Nodes list has four rows before its first node - the filter row, the sort row, the Map and Waypoints
# (MESH_UI_NODES_LEAD_ROWS) - so a node's row is its index in the demo roster plus four. Echo
# Repeater is seeds[5] and row 9; Golf Cabin is seeds[7] and row 11.

scene demo
tab nodes

# Echo Repeater, traced first. Right walks the detail a card at a time, and the two route cards
# are the first groups after the verbs: the way out, the way back, and when it was measured.
key down 9
key a
hold 1200
key right
hold 1200
key right
hold 2000
key b

# Golf Cabin, the trace the slot is still on - the one node the old client could draw. B left
# the cursor on Echo's own row, so this is two steps down the list rather than an index into it.
key down 2
key a
hold 1200
key right
hold 1200
key right
hold 2000
